menu "ps_can (TWAI transport)"

    config PS_CAN_TX_GPIO
        int "Default CAN TX GPIO"
        default 4
        help
            Bench default for the single-controller nodes (1-6). The chest hub
            passes both controllers' pins explicitly from board_hub.h instead.

    config PS_CAN_RX_GPIO
        int "Default CAN RX GPIO"
        default 5

    config PS_CAN_BITRATE
        int "CAN bitrate (bit/s)"
        range 25000 1000000
        default 1000000
        help
            Contract value is 1 Mbps on both buses (docs/network-map.md §2).
            The bus load budget in §10 assumes it; anything lower is a bench
            setting, not a suit setting. Every node on a segment must agree.

            Bench note: the SN65HVD230 modules in docs/bringup.md A.1 run in
            slope-control mode (Rs reported fixed at 10 kOhm, ~15 V/us, ~100 ns
            loop delay). TI specifies the part to 1 Mbps in that mode, and two
            nodes over 20 cm need ~200 ns of a ~750 ns sample point, so 1 Mbps
            is in spec. If bus_errors climb anyway, 250000 is the fallback:
            BENCH_CAN_BITRATE=250000 bash firmware/tools/build_bench.sh

endmenu
